rlm-harness
===========

This directory is a VENDORED COPY of `rlm`, the recursive language model CLI agent
by Prime Intellect:

    upstream:  https://github.com/PrimeIntellect-ai/rlm
    commit:    476b598
    license:   MIT (see LICENSE — Copyright (c) 2026 Prime Intellect)

We vendor rather than depend on it so that the exact agent loop used to produce the
paper's results is pinned in-tree and reproducible without a network fetch.

Local modifications
-------------------

One feature was added on top of upstream @476b598:

  * RLM_MAX_TURNS forced-finalize (`src/rlm/engine.py`). When the env var is set to
    N > 0, the engine caps the episode at N turns. On the final allowed turn it
    sends the request WITHOUT tools and injects a user notice beginning
    "FINAL TURN: ...", so the model must commit a plain-text final answer rather
    than continuing to call tools. TimeRLM uses N=15 during RL post-training, and
    the injected notice is what the taskset's -0.25 `forced_final_penalty` reward
    keys on (see environments/timeseries_qa_v1/timeseries_qa_v1/taskset.py).

The patch is confined to the turn loop in `engine.py`; every other file is upstream
as-is. Upstream's own repository scaffolding (CI workflows, pre-commit config, and
agent-instruction files) has been removed, as it does not apply to a vendored
subdirectory.
